# {{ .Name }}

A anywaye platform app, scaffolded by `cafe new --template platform`. It runs on
`cafe dev` with the launch four — identity, gateway, courier, and parlor —
composed into a starting product, ships from a Helm chart `cafe gen chart`
writes, and is held to the anywaye contract by `cafe contract lint`.

## The loop

```sh
cafe dev              # build the image and run the stack locally
cafe gen chart        # the Helm chart this app deploys from
cafe contract lint .  # the manifest, checked against core's schema
```

## What is in the box

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `anywaye.yml` | the app's identity: name, language, contract version, owner, repository, and the four platform dependencies |
| `main.go` | a real service on `:8080`, answering `/healthz` and `/readyz` |
| `go.mod` | the Go module |
| `docker/Dockerfile` | the image `cafe dev` builds, in the place it looks for one |

The app listens on 8080 because that is the port anywaye knows a Go service
listens on — it is read out of the manifest's `language`, not configured
anywhere, so the manifest and the container cannot disagree.

## The launch four

This app depends on the four platform services:

| Service | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| **identity** | authentication, sessions, MFA, accounts, tenancy |
| **gateway** | the front door / BFF — the only door in |
| **courier** | email through multiple providers |
| **parlor** | the web app the customer sees |

Each is declared in `anywaye.yml` under `dependencies` and resolved through the
service registry at `cafe dev` time. The registry (pantry serves the official
one) knows how to run each service locally; `cafe dev` starts them alongside
this app and wires the connections.

## The two rules that matter most

**The manifest is identity, not configuration.** Core's schema is
`additionalProperties: false`: a field core has not declared is an error, and
`cafe contract lint` reports it. A credential belongs in the deployment's
secret store, referenced by name — never in a file that is committed. When
this app starts publishing events or serving an API, declare them in
`exposes`: every event type opens with the publisher's own name, and
`cafe contract lint` enforces that too.

**The app is the editable surface.** The customer's repository is the source
of truth; the platform's surface is its contracts and configuration. An agent
that patches vendored platform service source creates a fork that has to be
supported through every update. Extend this app through the contract
(`anywaye.yml`, the OpenAPI document, the event types), not by editing the
platform underneath it.
